  "_doc": "A run follows one timeline. Rates are spawns/second as [time, value] keyframes (linear interpolation). Sector tier and endless cycle scale the whole thing via 'scaling': multiplier = 1 + per_tier * n + per_tier_sq * n^2, where n = tier - 1. The squared term keeps late sectors ahead of a fully upgraded player. A track or event with 'min_sector' only exists from that sector on, which is how later sectors add new enemies and set pieces instead of only bigger numbers; from 'mutator_start' each sector also carries one or two mutators (see 'sectors').",

